## Show Udhaar List on Frontend

This guide shows how to fetch and render the Udhaar (loan) list in your frontend app.

### Prerequisites

- **Auth**: Use a valid Bearer token (Sanctum). Include `Authorization: Bearer <token>` in all requests.
- **Base URL**: `/api`
- Backend routes are already defined:

```116:124:routes/api.php
    // Udhaar (Loan) Routes
    Route::apiResource('udhaars', UdhaarController::class);
    Route::post('/udhaars/{id}/repayments', [UdhaarController::class, 'recordRepayment']);
    Route::get('/udhaars/{id}/repayments', [UdhaarController::class, 'listRepayments']);
    Route::put('/udhaars/repayments/{repaymentId}', [UdhaarController::class, 'updateRepayment']);
    Route::delete('/udhaars/repayments/{repaymentId}', [UdhaarController::class, 'deleteRepayment']);
    Route::get('/udhaars/summary', [UdhaarController::class, 'summary']);
    Route::get('/udhaars/user/{userId}/summary', [UdhaarController::class, 'userSummary']);
```

### List Endpoint

- **Method**: GET `-/api/udhaars`
- **Query params (optional)**:
  - `user_id`: number
  - `status`: `active | fully_paid | cancelled`
  - `start_date`: `YYYY-MM-DD`
  - `end_date`: `YYYY-MM-DD`
  - `page`: number (default 1)
  - `per_page`: number (default 15)

